  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 6,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.049,
            0.432,
            0.066
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.088,
            0.847,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This problem also can be solved using the fact that addition and subtraction are inverse operations. However, we can use the following method that is perhaps easier to visualise."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.146,
            0.847,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To retain only the expression to be evaluated on the LHS, we need to remove the term –(–67). We can remove this term by adding (–67) to both sides of the equation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.203,
            0.709,
            0.222
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_3.jpg",
          "content": "12345-5432+132-24-(-67)+(-67)=7091+(-67)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.222,
            0.709,
            0.241
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_4.jpg",
          "content": "12345-5432+132-24-(-6\\mathcal{J})+(-6\\mathcal{J})=7091+(-67)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.242,
            0.51,
            0.26
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "12345-5432+132-24=7024."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.272,
            0.847,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 4:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " It is known that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\cfrac { 3 5 } { 1 1 3 } } \\right) \\times 2 4 \\times 1 4 \\times \\left( { \\cfrac { 8 } { 9 } } \\right) = { \\cfrac { 9 4 0 8 0 } { 1 0 1 7 } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . What is the value of the expression "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\cfrac { 3 5 } { 1 1 3 } } \\right) \\times 2 4 \\times 1 4 ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.349,
            0.844,
            0.408
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solution:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " To retain only the expression to be evaluated on the LHS we need to remove the factor "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\frac { 8 } { 9 } } \\right)"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " . We can do that by dividing both sides by "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\left( { \\frac { 8 } { 9 } } \\right)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.308,
            0.415,
            0.69,
            0.456
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_8.jpg",
          "content": "\\left[ \\left( \\frac{35}{113} \\right) \\times 24 \\times 14 \\times \\left( \\frac{8}{9} \\right) \\right] \\div \\left( \\frac{8}{9} \\right) = \\frac{94080}{1017} \\div \\left( \\frac{8}{9} \\right)"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.467,
            0.678,
            0.508
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_9.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{35}{113} \\right) \\times 24 \\times 14 \\times \\left( \\frac{8}{9} \\right) \\times \\left( \\frac{9}{8} \\right) = \\frac{94080}{1017} \\times \\left( \\frac{9}{8} \\right)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.52,
            0.211,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.316,
            0.551,
            0.546,
            0.589
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_6_equation_11.jpg",
          "content": "\\left( \\frac{35}{113} \\right) \\times 24 \\times 14 = \\frac{11760}{113}"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.59,
            0.669,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us use these ideas to solve the equation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x - 4 = 7."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.616,
            0.846,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What can we do so that 5x is on one side and the equality between the LHS and the RHS still holds?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.654,
            0.846,
            0.692
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To retain only 5x on the LHS, we need to remove the term – 4. This can be done by adding 4 to both sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.697,
            0.374,
            0.716
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x - 4 + 4 = 7 \\pm 4."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.722,
            0.303,
            0.741
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Hence, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "5x = 11."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.746,
            0.846,
            0.785
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To retain only the unknown x on the LHS, we need to remove the factor 5. This can be done by dividing both sides by 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.79,
            0.293,
            0.826
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 x } { 5 } = \\frac { 1 1 } { 5 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.831,
            0.257,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "x = { \\frac { 1 1 } { 5 } }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.933,
            0.194,
            0.95
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "170"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
